  DELIVERY-FREE d42a statement: over its 36-state exhaustive family the
  per-state menu mass takes exactly two values, 2 and 5/2, and the excess 1/2
  appears exactly where a blind conflict group becomes visible in the join
  view.  THIS record is at TRANSPORT scope with M actors and an open delivery
  sector, so the masses are NOT the same numbers and are not compared as such.
  The commensurable quantity is the LADDER EXCESS: d42b1 prices each actor's
  menu at 1 + (m - 1)/4 with m the number of distinct ckey groups (plus the
  merge sector) visible to it, so mass - M, in units of 1/4, COUNTS the extra
  visible conflict groups.  D65's 5/2 over two actors is an excess of two
  quarters; the census below is of exactly that quantity, at this scope.
